{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     139 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md\n     1\t# judging-v13: related number questions judged together, with a checked calculation (design v2, for council round 46b)\n     2\t\n     3\tOpened by Alex (D726) for the bounded test of D725. Harness-only until a later decision: no product configuration names it, and\n     4\tthe ordinary launchers refuse it (D359, D723). The frozen judge (judging-v7, poc-v118) is unchanged.\n     5\t\n     6\tv2 answers round 46 (`codex-r46.md`), findings 1–6. The changes are marked [46.n].\n     7\t\n     8\t## 1. What changes\n     9\t\n    10\t| Piece | judging-v7 (today) | judging-v13 |\n    11\t|---|---|---|\n    12\t| Unit | one question per call | one **family** per call: the number questions of one company whose quantities overlap (a total and its segment or product line, a level and its growth, and a later year declared to rest on an earlier year's base [46.2]). Each keeps its own answer |\n    13\t| Who forms a family | none (0 dependencies) | **declared** for the test from the stored cases, with typed relations: `part_of(part, whole)` and `same_base(later, earlier)`. Production would need a matching version that names them |\n    14\t| Evidence shown | each question's own evidence in view (D198) | the union of the members' evidence in view, each passage once with its attribution; themes once |\n    15\t| Previous conclusion | rung and reasons, cut at 800 characters, unmarked | each member's previous rung and outcome, labelled \"our earlier forecast, not a source\". It can enter a calculation only as a `prior_forecast` figure (§2), never as a source or a market reference |\n    16\t| Answer | prose fields plus one answer-wide citation list | a calculation (figures) plus exactly one answer per member (§2) |\n    17\t| Request text | judging-v7 | a full v13 request written and audited (§5) [46.6] |\n    18\t| Failure | refused twice: the question is left as it was | refused twice: the family is recorded **unresolved** and no member is updated. A member may also answer `unresolved` itself (§2) [46.5] |\n    19\t\n    20\t## 2. The answer format (closed set; the schema enforces shape, code enforces §3)\n    21\t\n    22\t```\n    23\tfigures: [ { id,\n    24\t             what: { population, measure, scope, period },     # canonical: measure is the quantity (\"revenue\"), not its basis [46.1]\n    25\t             basis: \"reported\" | \"guidance\" | \"consensus\" | \"third_party\" | \"forecast\" | \"prior_forecast\",\n    26\t             scenario: \"base\" | \"<named>\",                       # default \"base\" [46.1]\n    27\t             kind: \"source\" | \"computed\" | \"estimate\",\n    28\t             value | {low, high} | {bound: \">\" | \">=\" | \"<\" | \"<=\" | \"~\", value},  unit,\n    29\t             # kind source:   evidence: \"<id>\", span: \"<exact substring of the shown quote>\"            [46.4]\n    30\t             # kind computed: inputs: [...], operation: sum|difference|product|ratio|growth|apply_growth|share|range_from_relative,\n    31\t             #                relation (sum only): \"accounting_parts\" | \"stated_in_addition\" | \"overlap_unknown\",\n    32\t             #                bridge (when inputs' what differ from the output's): \"<figure id of an estimate>\"   [46.3]\n    33\t             # kind estimate: basis_text, rests_on: [figure ids, evidence ids],\n    34\t             #                adjusts (optional): { figure: \"<id>\", type: \"discount\" | \"uplift\" | \"trim\" | \"range_around\" }  [46.3]\n    35\t           } ]\n    36\tanswers: [ { view_id,\n    37\t             uses: [ forecast figure ids, one per period the answer depends on ],   # [46.1]\n    38\t             outcome: \"<figure id>\" | null, unresolved: false | { why },          # [46.5]\n    39\t             reference: { figure: \"<id>\" } | { unavailable: \"<why>\" },            # per answer [46.2]\n    40\t             rung, reasons, cites, pushes, theme_pushes, changed, why_changed } ]\n    41\t```\n    42\t\n    43\t- **An arithmetic intermediate and the analyst's final range are distinct figures** [46.2]. For example, q02's $392B × 92% is a\n    44\t  `computed` figure. The final $370–400B is an `estimate` resting on it and on q01's range. Code checks the intermediate's arithmetic\n    45\t  and never requires the final range to equal it.\n    46\t- **`prior_forecast`** is a figure the system forecast earlier. It may feed a declared `same_base` (q22 reuses q01's FY2027 base) and\n    47\t  stays labelled as the system's own.\n    48\t\n    49\t## 3. What code checks (identity and arithmetic only)\n    50\t\n    51\t| Check | Rule | Refuses |\n    52\t|---|---|---|\n    53\t| **C1 source span** [46.4] | `span` is an exact substring of the cited passage as shown. It parses, by the closed forms below, to exactly the figure's value, unit, sign and qualifier: no tolerance. Points: \"$108.0 billion\" = 108 USD bn. Ranges: \"$105–110 billion\". Bounds: \"more than $730 billion\" is (>730), \"nearly $800 billion\" is (~<800), \"at least\" is (>=). Relative: \"plus or minus 2%\" is ±2%. Words: \"double\" = ×2, \"more than double\" = (>×2), \"triple\" = ×3. Any other wording cannot be a source figure; it stays evidence the estimate cites | an amount absent from its span; a span absent from the passage; a wrong number within 0.5% (108.5 for \"$108.0 billion\"); a bound written as a point |\n    54\t| **C2 arithmetic** | a `computed` figure recomputes from its inputs by its operation. Rounding: to the figure's stated precision, at most 0.5% or 0.1 unit. `range_from_relative` makes 108 ± 2% into 105.84–110.16 | a wrong sum, share or endpoint |\n    55\t| **C3 part within whole** [46.1] | for each `part_of` relation, for every period both members `use`, in the same scenario: the part's forecast is at most the whole's. For ranges, part.low ≤ whole.low and part.high ≤ whole.high. Annual and every quarter are compared when both state them | a segment quarter above the company quarter |\n    56\t| **C4 one forecast per quantity** [46.1] | within a scenario, at most one `basis: forecast` figure per `what`. Every member that depends on a period of a shared quantity `uses` that figure. A guide (`basis: guidance`) and a forecast of the same quarter may coexist | two members forecasting one quarter with different values |\n    57\t| **C5 reference** [46.2] | each answer's reference is either a `source` figure whose basis is consensus, guidance or third_party from a passage whose speaker is not the system, or a `computed` figure every leaf of which is such a source (q02's consensus × mix), or `unavailable` with a reason. No leaf may be `prior_forecast` or `forecast` | the system's own forecast presented as the market's |\n    58\t| **C6 rung and outcome** [46.2] | the chosen rung's band overlaps the outcome (a point: contains it). The reasons say why that band, where the range overlaps several | a rung no part of the outcome falls in |\n    59\t| **C7 structure** [46.5] | exactly one answer per member; an answer's outcome `what` matches its member's question (population, measure, scope, period, from the question's typed key); figure ids are unique; references are not dangling and not circular; operations come from the closed set | a missing or doubled member, a borrowed outcome, a dangling or circular figure |\n    60\t| **C8 bridge** [46.3] | a `computed` figure whose inputs' `what` differ from its own in population, scope or period, other than by a declared `part_of` or `same_base`, names a `bridge` estimate that states the conversion | 730/800 × $1.3T with no stated assumption that four companies' 2026 spending share carries to five companies' 2027 capex |\n    61\t\n    62\t**Recorded, not refused** (visible to readers and to the page) [46.3]:\n    63\t- **Overlap:** a `sum` with relation `overlap_unknown`. Its alternate drops the disputed addend.\n    64\t- **Adjustment:** an `estimate` that `adjusts` a figure (a discount, uplift or trim). Its alternate is the adjusted figure itself.\n    65\t  R4: the guided bound (>40).\n    66\t- **Bridge:** every bridge. Its alternate is undetermined.\n    67\t- **Band-deciding:** code recomputes the outcome under each defined alternate, the other assumptions fixed, and records the\n    68\t  assumption as band-deciding when the rung changes. Where no alternate is defined, it records \"undetermined\". A reader decides\n    69\t  whether a band-deciding assumption is supported. D721/D722: unresolved inclusion is never treated as proof of double counting.\n    70\t\n    71\t**The model keeps:** drivers, weights, discounts, scenarios, the choice among overlapping bands, and whether to step off the\n    72\treference. Code never prefers guidance, prescribes a haircut, refuses an estimate for being one, or picks a band from a midpoint.\n    73\t\n    74\t## 4. Tables\n    75\t\n    76\t**Value × reader.**\n    77\t- **The calculation, the recorded assumptions and band-deciding flags:** read by the checks, the readers' packets, and later the\n    78\t  page.\n    79\t- **`unresolved`:** read by the round (no member updated) and the bundle (\"Forecast unavailable\", D726).\n    80\t- **The family declaration:** read by the request builder, C3, C4 and C7.\n    81\t- **Nothing in poc-v118 reads any of it.**\n    82\t\n    83\t**New path × old checks.**\n    84\t- v7's id, rung, push and theme checks apply per member answer. `cites` names shown evidence only.\n    85\t- `cites_views` is always empty.\n    86\t- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\n    87\t\n    88\t**State × event (the test harness).** Inputs are fixed: the stored requests' passages and the gold packet's items, as of the stored\n    89\tday.\n    90\t\n    91\t| Event | Outcome |\n    92\t|---|---|\n    93\t| success | the calculation and answers are recorded with their check results |\n    94\t| refusal | the errors are recorded; one retry with them |\n    95\t| second refusal | the family is unresolved, recorded |\n    96\t| a member's own `unresolved` | recorded; the others publish if they pass |\n    97\t| crash midway | the attempt is recorded incomplete and counts as no result |\n    98\t\n    99\tNothing writes a product store. Production lifecycle (members closing or opening, families changing) is designed only if the test\n   100\tpasses.\n   101\t\n   102\t**Prior decisions:**\n   103\t- D24, D28: bounded to the figures open questions consume.\n   104\t- D198: evidence in view, unioned.\n   105\t- D260, D263: the standard kept.\n   106\t- D359, D723: no product launcher.\n   107\t- D695: number questions.\n   108\t- D711, D721, D722: linking passed conclusions, and unresolved inclusion is not double counting.\n   109\t- D725, D726.\n   110\t\n   111\t## 5. The v13 request text (written and audited at $0 before the gate closes) [46.6]\n   112\t\n   113\t- **The basis:** judging-v7's standard sentences are kept, among them the reference, run-rate, discount, sizing, identities and\n   114\t  consistency.\n   115\t- **Replaced where they conflict with a family:**\n   116\t  - the single-question delivery (\"the current conclusions of dependencies\");\n   117\t  - \"the previous conclusion carries\" pieces not shown, which becomes \"our earlier forecast, not a source\";\n   118\t  - the one-reference, one-outcome output sentence;\n   119\t  - the dependency-consistency sentence, which becomes the family's own consistency, the same clause made family-wide.\n   120\t- **Added:** how to write figures (kinds, bases, spans, relations, bridges, `adjusts`, `unresolved`).\n   121\t- **The audit:** every changed sentence is shown with its source (D260, D263, D725, this design), read against a stored family\n   122\t  request, and its character count before and after is reported (AGENTS §6).\n   123\t\n   124\t## 6. The $0 gate (registered; each defect must produce its named finding) [46.5]\n   125\t\n   126\t| Item | Content | Pass: the named finding |\n   127\t|---|---|---|\n   128\t| R1a | old-2 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9) on 09-20, as stored: v9 Q4 146, v14 Q4 127 | **C3** on Q4 |\n   129\t| R1b | the same, with the Q3 forecasts as stored: v9 uses 99.9 (the guide midpoint × mix as its Q3 company base), v14 uses 113.5 | **C4** on Q3 company revenue, independent of C3 |\n   130\t| R1c (control) | a guide node (108 ± 2%, from e2499's span) beside one shared Q3 forecast node (113.5) used by both | passes |\n   131\t| R2 | old-2 8734: $25B (e2620) + $18B (e2889) written as `overlap_unknown`, + MediaTek, + talks as estimates | recorded overlap; band-deciding (about $35B, rung 2) |\n   132\t| R3 | old-2 8595: 730 (e1786, a bound: >730) / 800 (e2535, ~<800) × 1,300 | **C1** if bounds are used as points; with bounds kept, **C8** without a bridge; with a bridge: recorded, alternate undetermined |\n   133\t| R4 | old-3 9166: \">2 × 20\" (e3660, \"more than double\") gives >40, trimmed to 38–39 by `adjusts: trim` | recorded adjustment, band-deciding (>40 is rung 2) |\n   134\t| G1–G4 (controls) | q01, q02, q19, q22, written from `gold-v1.json`'s reasoning (spans from the packet items) | all pass, estimates visible; q02's derived reference passes C5; q19's overlapping range passes C6 with its reason; q22's `same_base` uses q01's forecast |\n   135\t| P1–P3 (plants, on control copies) | an amount absent from its span; a wrong sum; a prior forecast as the reference | P1 **C1**, P2 **C2**, P3 **C5**, each for its intended reason |\n   136\t| T1–T4 (C1 forms, real passages) | e2499 \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\"; e1786 \"more than $730 billion\"; e3660 \"more than double\"; 108.5 against e2499 | parse as stated; T4 refused |\n   137\t\n   138\t- **Stop:** any missing finding, a finding for the wrong reason, or a control the format cannot express.\n   139\t- **Then:** Council B on the gate's output. The paid gate's ceiling goes to Alex.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'C[1-8]|\\\\[46\\\\.|#' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46*.md; sed -n '10957,11018p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '1,13p;78,94p' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md; rg -n 'rung|first judgement|prior' src/hivemind/views/judging.py | tail -17\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'C[1-8]|\\\\[46\\\\.|#' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46*.md; sed -n '10957,11018p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '1,13p;78,94p' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md; rg -n 'rung|first judgement|prior' src/hivemind/views/judging.py | tail -17\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46-brief.md:1:# Council round 46: review the judging-v13 design before its $0 gate (read-only, same thread)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46-brief.md:9:2. Do C1–C6 and the two \"recorded\" lists catch the five stored cases as §5 registers, without refusing valid reasoning?\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46-brief.md:11:4. Is C1's text matching sound against the real passages? Consider ranges, \"±2%\", \"over $730 billion\" and numbers written in words.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46-brief.md:12:5. Is C4's key (population, measure, scope, period) enough to tell a guide from a forecast of the same quarter, or a scenario from the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46b-brief.md:1:# Council round 46b: review design v2 (read-only, same thread)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46b-brief.md:3:Claude revised `DESIGN.md` to v2 against your round 46. The changes are marked [46.n]. Check that each finding is answered without\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round46b-brief.md:4:creating a new serious defect. Read the real passages behind C1 (old-2 e2499, e1786, e2535, e2620, e2889; old-3 e3660).\n## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n    ceiling.\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\n# Why the number answers cannot be trusted: council round 45/45b (2026-11-22, consensus, $0)\n\nAlex asked to step back and find which part of the design produces the unreliable numbers. The record:\n- `round45-brief.md`;\n- `claude-r45.md` (written before Codex);\n- `codex-r45.md` (an independent investigation, fresh thread `01a20501…`, read-only, no model calls);\n- `round45b-brief.md` and `codex-r45b.md` (the challenge round).\n\n## The answer\n\nThe system has no single, checked calculation behind its related numbers:\n- **Each number question is judged alone.** It rebuilds the company's numbers from its own slice of evidence, with its own bases and\n  its own reference.\n## The one test (registered with the design)\n\n- **The $0 gate.** Hand-reconstruct, in the new format:\n  - old-2 8729/8737, 8734 and 8595, and old-3 9166;\n  - the four gold controls;\n  - three planted errors (an amount absent from its quote, a wrong sum, an internal forecast labelled consensus).\n\n  The format must expose every defect, represent every control, and fail every plant. Any miss stops the line.\n- **The paid gate** (Alex's ceiling; 36 calls, about $0.2–0.4 estimated):\n  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\n    format and checks. Plus three samples each on the O, S and E requests. Every output is read against its source with the arm\n    hidden.\n  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\n    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\n    unresolved overlap, scope or unsized adjustments that decide the band.\n  - **Stop:** any such published defect, either coverage line missed, or an incomplete comparison.\n175:             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n198:            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n200:                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n202:            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n208:            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n211:        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n213:        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n230:    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n235:    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes, hidden=hidden,\n283:    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n284:    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n285:        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n300:        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n301:    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n302:        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n308:    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n316:    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import pathlib, sqlite3, json, re\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\\\\'').resolve()\ndef con(i,t):\n c=sqlite3.connect((root/f'\\\\''old-{i}/prod/{t}.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef archival(i,cid,eids):\n a=con(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n r=a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,request_json,answer_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()\n j=con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,view_id from judgements where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()\n assert r[0]==j[0]\n t=json.loads(r[1])['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n print(i,cid,j[1])\n for eid in eids:\n  m=re.search(r'\\\\''\"'^- '\"'\\\\''+eid+r'\\\\'' \\\\[.*\\\\n    Quote: (.*)\"'$'\"'\\\\'',t,re.M); assert m\n  e=con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select quote from evidence where evidence_id=?'\\\\'',(eid,)).fetchone()\n  assert m[1]==e[0][:400]\n  print(eid,m[1])\n ans=json.loads(r[2])\n print(ans['\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\''])\n if cid==9166:\n  print(ans['\\\\''reference'\\\\''])\n  for row in con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select position,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\'',(j[1],)):\n   print(tuple(row))\nfor i,cid,eids in [(2,8729,['\\\\''e2499'\\\\'']),(2,8595,['\\\\''e1786'\\\\'','\\\\''e2535'\\\\'']),(2,8734,['\\\\''e2620'\\\\'','\\\\''e2889'\\\\'']),(3,9166,['\\\\''e3660'\\\\'']),(2,8737,['\\\\''e3219'\\\\''])]:\n archival(i,cid,eids)\np=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold'\\\\'')\nfor item in json.loads((p/'\\\\''packet-v1.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''items'\\\\'']:\n if item['\\\\''id'\\\\''] in {'\\\\''i037'\\\\'','\\\\''i090'\\\\'','\\\\''i129'\\\\'','\\\\''i218'\\\\'','\\\\''i281'\\\\''}: print(item['\\\\''id'\\\\''],item['\\\\''tier'\\\\''],item['\\\\''passage'\\\\''])\ng={e['\\\\''question_id'\\\\'']:e for e in json.loads((p/'\\\\''gold-v1.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''entries'\\\\'']}\nprint('\\\\''q02 reference'\\\\'',g['\\\\''q02'\\\\'']['\\\\''reference'\\\\'']['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\nprint('\\\\''q22 reasoning'\\\\'',g['\\\\''q22'\\\\'']['\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\'']['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import pathlib, sqlite3, json, re\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\\\\'').resolve()\ndef con(i,t):\n c=sqlite3.connect((root/f'\\\\''old-{i}/prod/{t}.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef archival(i,cid,eids):\n a=con(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n r=a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,request_json,answer_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()\n j=con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,view_id from judgements where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()\n assert r[0]==j[0]\n t=json.loads(r[1])['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n print(i,cid,j[1])\n for eid in eids:\n  m=re.search(r'\\\\''\"'^- '\"'\\\\''+eid+r'\\\\'' \\\\[.*\\\\n    Quote: (.*)\"'$'\"'\\\\'',t,re.M); assert m\n  e=con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select quote from evidence where evidence_id=?'\\\\'',(eid,)).fetchone()\n  assert m[1]==e[0][:400]\n  print(eid,m[1])\n ans=json.loads(r[2])\n print(ans['\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\''])\n if cid==9166:\n  print(ans['\\\\''reference'\\\\''])\n  for row in con(i,'\\\\''views'\\\\'').execute('\\\\''select position,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\'',(j[1],)):\n   print(tuple(row))\nfor i,cid,eids in [(2,8729,['\\\\''e2499'\\\\'']),(2,8595,['\\\\''e1786'\\\\'','\\\\''e2535'\\\\'']),(2,8734,['\\\\''e2620'\\\\'','\\\\''e2889'\\\\'']),(3,9166,['\\\\''e3660'\\\\'']),(2,8737,['\\\\''e3219'\\\\''])]:\n archival(i,cid,eids)\np=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold'\\\\'')\nfor item in json.loads((p/'\\\\''packet-v1.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''items'\\\\'']:\n if item['\\\\''id'\\\\''] in {'\\\\''i037'\\\\'','\\\\''i090'\\\\'','\\\\''i129'\\\\'','\\\\''i218'\\\\'','\\\\''i281'\\\\''}: print(item['\\\\''id'\\\\''],item['\\\\''tier'\\\\''],item['\\\\''passage'\\\\''])\ng={e['\\\\''question_id'\\\\'']:e for e in json.loads((p/'\\\\''gold-v1.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''entries'\\\\'']}\nprint('\\\\''q02 reference'\\\\'',g['\\\\''q02'\\\\'']['\\\\''reference'\\\\'']['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\nprint('\\\\''q22 reasoning'\\\\'',g['\\\\''q22'\\\\'']['\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\'']['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"2 8729 v14\ne2499 Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\nAbout $419 billion: Q1 $81.6 billion plus Q2 $96.2 billion, estimated Q3 of about $113.5 billion (the $110.16 billion guidance high end plus the reported average 3.1% beat), and Q4 of about $127 billion by carrying forward the guided 12% sequential growth.\n2 8595 v6\ne1786 Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will spend more than $730 billion combined on AI infrastructure this year, and they expect that number to increase next year.\ne2535 With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\nAbout $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate $730 billion/$800 billion four-to-five share proxy to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five calendar-2027 CapEx estimate (e2535; repeated in e4756 and later reports).\n2 8734 v29\ne2620 These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\ne2889 The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.\nAbout $53 billion: $25 billion of commitments reported as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, then the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced after that remainder-of-year figure and a risk-adjusted contribution from the $10 billion Anthropic and $2.5 billion Thinking Machines discussions.\n3 9166 v41\ne3660 The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CPU revenue in its fiscal 2027, but expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028.\nRoughly $38–39 billion for FY2028: the stated more-than-double expectation points above $40 billion, but is discounted for a forward Vera target without shipment volume in hand, with the competitive evidence adding execution risk.\nNVIDIA management’s stated expectation that FY2028 CPU revenue will more than double the $20 billion FY2027 expectation implies more than $40 billion, which is rung 2.\n(1, 50000000000.0, None)\n(2, 40000000000.0, 50000000000.0)\n(3, 30000000000.0, 40000000000.0)\n(4, 20000000000.0, 30000000000.0)\n(5, None, 20000000000.0)\n2 8737 v9\ne3219 Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\nApproximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\ni037 third_party_view from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\ni090 third_party_view Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\ni129 fact During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\ni218 third_party_view The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\ni281 party_statement forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\nq02 reference No segment consensus is stated; consensus total revenue of $392bn (i037) at the Q1 Data Center share of 92% of sales (i129) implies about $360bn.\nq22 reasoning A higher FY2027 base of $400-435bn (q01: i295, i106) at the Street's 41% (i090) is $565-615bn; NVIDIA projects the big four's capex rising from $650bn to over $1 trillion in 2027 (i256, i173), a 54% step; Huang's $1 trillion of Blackwell and Rubin sales through 2027 (i079) exceeds consensus total revenue over the window; Rubin racks sell at about twice the GB300 price (i216) and Vera CPUs add a line (i288). Against: the Kyber rack may slip to 2028 (i100) with Oberon-Rubin racks filling the gap (i181), and memory stays tight until 2028 (i252). I bet $560-640bn.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"NOT READY\n\nV2 fixes the midpoint rule and gives each answer its own comparison. The gate still admits the **same $108B versus $113.5B Q3 split** it is meant to catch, and C5 rejects q02’s valid gold comparison.\n\n1. **C3/C4 still trust the answer’s list of inputs.** In R1b, **$99.9B is Data Center revenue**. Its company-wide input is the **$108B guide**. V14 uses **$113.5B** as its company forecast. Under C4, v9 can use a `guidance` node and v14 a `forecast` node, leaving only one forecast node for C4 to check. V9 could also list the shared forecast in `uses` while its calculation still reads the guide. C3 likewise compares only periods both members list. **Fix I’d accept:** bind the required shared quantities and periods in the test declaration. Check the inputs that actually feed each outcome, in the same published scenario. R1b must fail with the guide still correctly labelled, and listing an unused shared node must not cure it. For ranges, compare explicitly paired scenarios or a declared calculation that preserves the part-to-whole relationship. Matching low and high endpoints alone leaves the pairing unknown. [Design C3–C4 and R1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:55), [Old-2 calls 8729 and 8737](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite)\n\n2. **C1 lets a shorter quote turn a bound into a point.** I checked the six passages in the archived requests. In `e1786`, `$730 billion` is an exact substring of **more than $730 billion**. The same problem applies to **nearly $800 billion** in `e2535` and **more than double** in `e3660`. The schema also has no defined form for C1’s `~<800`. `e2499` gives a **$108B midpoint with ±2% guidance**. The midpoint is a valid input in that role, and the endpoints are calculated. Finally, `e2620` gives **$25B of commitments** alongside **$99B of investments**, while `e2889` puts **$18B** on top of **$47.9B already held**. That last passage establishes no addition to the $25B. **Fix I’d accept:** validate a complete numeric expression at a specific quote occurrence, including its qualifiers and unit. Define the representations for approximate bounds, relative ranges, and multipliers. Allow the midpoint as an explicitly identified component of the guidance. Add gate checks that try to strip the qualifiers from these real passages. Keep the scope and overlap reading separate from the literal-number check. [Design C1 and T1–T4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:53), [Old-2 calls 8729, 8595 and 8734](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite), [Old-3 call 9166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/archive.sqlite)\n\n3. **C5 and C8 still conflict with the gold controls.** C5 allows only consensus, guidance, or third-party inputs in a derived comparison. **q02 uses a reported 92% mix** from `i129`, so it fails as written. Meanwhile, C8 can demand an estimate to bridge q01’s Q1 and Q2 into H1 because the periods differ, even though that is ordinary addition of disjoint periods. In the other direction, C8 omits `measure` from its check and accepts a bridge that is just a pointer to an estimate. **Fix I’d accept:** allow a derived comparison anchored in outside expectations to use reported conversion inputs. Keep its provenance visible. Specify compatibility by operation: time aggregation needs matching quantities and disjoint periods, a share needs a defined numerator and denominator, and a change of spending measure, population, or period needs a conversion tied to the actual operands. In G4, bind **q22 to q01’s forecast at the same snapshot**. If the format also permits a prior-day forecast, require an exact dated pointer to the earlier answer supplied in the request. [Design §§2–3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:43), [Frozen gold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/gold-v1.json), [Gold source passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/packet-v1.json)\n\n4. **The sensitivity check still cannot compute the registered results.** `overlap_unknown` gives no operand to drop. If a later estimate only lists what it `rests_on`, code cannot recalculate that estimate after changing an input. R4 also claims **“>40 is rung 2”**, but call **9166** has rung 2 at **$40B to below $50B** and rung 1 at **$50B or more**. The undiscounted bound proves a crossing of $40B, with no unique alternate rung. **Fix I’d accept:** name the disputed operand and the explicit alternate calculation. R2 can omit the $18B while holding the other adjustments fixed, yielding about $35B as a conditional result. For bounds or ranges, record the boundary that definitely or possibly changes. Where a downstream estimate has no formula or R3 has no defensible alternate, record **undetermined** and keep the assumption visible to the reader. Use recomputed values for boundary checks and round only for display. [Design recorded assumptions and gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:62), [Old-3 call 9166 and stored bands](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite)\n\n5. **The unresolved answer still conflicts with the old checks and the state table.** The schema retains `rung` while permitting a null outcome, and §4 applies the old rung checks to every member. One row says unresolved updates no member. Another lets other members publish, without saying what happens if their calculation needs the unresolved member. **Fix I’d accept:** define two answer shapes. A forecast has an outcome and rung. An unresolved answer has a reason and neither. For this harness, hold the affected family whenever a required shared input or reconciliation is unresolved. Exercise a member-declared unresolved answer and the repeated-refusal path before the gate can pass. [Design answer format and state table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:36)\n\n**Wording-level notes**\n\n- In §2, q02’s $370–400B forecast uses q01’s forecast and the estimated segment share. The $392B × 92% calculation supplies its comparison.\n- §5 addresses the earlier prompt conflict at the design level. Include the full request and schema audit in the gate record, as §5 specifies."}}
